      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T16:46:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The allowlist here accepts kernel, dnvme, nvme-cli, tnvme, open-osd as valid dependency sources, but only qemu/simulator are folded into branches/dependencies for the artifact identity - so two builds differing only in, say, a kernel or open-osd dependency would produce the same artifact key and be treated as reusable. If the QEMU binary genuinely can\u0027t depend on those, please assert/comment that explicitly; otherwise this should be rejected rather than silently accepted and dropped.",
